  is ever reachable through an ingress, LB, or a dev tunnel, the route is simply public.

  The dashboard team's actual problem is that a script can't hold a browser session cookie. That's solvable without
  opening the route: accept a service token alongside the cookie, so scripts authenticate and humans keep using login.
  It's still about one line in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m plus an env var.
